@wsycqyz, thank you for the detailed review. Both findings are addressed in the latest revision (`0f89dc533`):

- non-positive, unreadable, and non-finite watt readings now use the DUT-status fallback;
- the fallback validates aggregate PSU health and redundancy without matching PDU graph labels to DUT PSU names.

The PR body now includes the updated focused checks and physical evidence: Testplan ID `6acf0edcb4b89a8641b012f2`, target 2/2 passed, overall 18 pass / 3 skip / 0 failure / 0 error. Fresh CI is running against the new head. Could you please review the latest revision when you have a chance?

@peterbailey-arista @deepak-singhal0408 @venu-nexthop @StormLiangMS @lolyu @yutongzhang-microsoft please review.

This change replaces fixed waits with route-convergence checks, shuts the whole PortChannel when needed to remove an ECMP path, and prepares the expected routes before the flap so both route checks and traffic use the intended outcome. It also avoids writing FIB data to a file only to read it back. The latest revision retains the original cleanup behavior and `upstream_lc` naming to keep the scope and diff focused.

The earlier revision passed 20 runs on 720DT MX and 5 on 7260 LAG: https://github.com/sonic-net/sonic-mgmt/pull/28331#issuecomment-6014789118. Those results predate the cleanup adjustment. I am preparing a 10-run Elastictest plan on 720DT MX for the current code and will add its URL and results here once available.

