@StormLiangMS @lolyu @wsycqyz please review this NIC-simulator hardening change. The reproduced failure occurred on a server where OVS-backed simulator startup took much longer than the fixed five-second sleep; the underlying reason that server is slow is tracked separately in https://msazure.visualstudio.com/One/_workitems/edit/39676296. This PR reduces unnecessary OVS work, while https://github.com/sonic-net/sonic-mgmt/pull/27928 adds the separate RPC-readiness barrier.

I am not familiar with this part of the simulator and did my best to trace the state transitions, review the failure/retry paths, and test the combined correction. In traces from nine actual SNMP runs, 501 forwarding-state SET requests produced 432 `mod-group` writes, avoiding 69 unchanged writes (13.77%; 4–12 per run).

@vaibhavhd please also review the 202605 backport request. This hardening stabilizes the active-active Dual-ToR test setup on slow servers; target-branch validation evidence is linked in the description.

